From: h713 <h713@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT: give DECD exclusive ownership without display reset

This is scaffolding for one controlled DECD frame-submit test.  The normal
H713 DT deliberately gives AFBD MMIO 0x05600000 and SPI 110 to the KMS driver
and disables DECD.  Enabling DECD alongside KMS would create two owners for
the same registers and interrupt, so swap the owner for this boot.

The display was adopted from U-Boot and Linux cannot reconstruct it after a
shared display reset.  Withhold rst_bus_disp from DECD and make that reset
optional in the reconstructed driver.  reset_control_*() is a no-op for the
NULL optional handle.  Do not issue PM_HINT off or unload the module during
the test: those operations also disable shared display clocks.

OUT OF SERIES.  This boot has no KMS device or framebuffer console.  Use the
serial console, load sunxi-decd.ko deliberately, submit one synthetic frame,
and reboot afterward.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
@@ -38,3 +38,18 @@
 &motor_ctr { status = "disabled"; };
 &adc_keys { status = "disabled"; };
 &board_mgr { status = "disabled"; };
+
+/*
+ * One-boot DECD experiment: KMS and DECD share AFBD MMIO and SPI 110, so
+ * exactly one may be enabled.  The adopted panel reset is intentionally not
+ * exposed to DECD; a reset would blank the projector until reboot.
+ */
+&display {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&dec {
+	/delete-property/ resets;
+	/delete-property/ reset-names;
+	status = "okay";
+};
diff --git a/drivers/misc/sunxi_decd/decd_core.c b/drivers/misc/sunxi_decd/decd_core.c
--- a/drivers/misc/sunxi_decd/decd_core.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/sunxi_decd/decd_core.c
@@ -117,7 +117,8 @@ int dec_init(struct dec_device *dec)
 	dec->clk_bus_disp = devm_clk_get(dev, "clk_bus_disp");
 	if (IS_ERR(dec->clk_bus_disp))
 		return PTR_ERR(dec->clk_bus_disp);
-	dec->rst_bus_disp = devm_reset_control_get_shared(dev, "rst_bus_disp");
+	dec->rst_bus_disp =
+		devm_reset_control_get_optional_shared(dev, "rst_bus_disp");
 	if (IS_ERR(dec->rst_bus_disp))
 		return PTR_ERR(dec->rst_bus_disp);
 
